+## Keys and roles
+
+Every request carries an API key:
+
+    Authorization: Bearer <key>
+
+Keys are stored in the data as `apiKeys: [{ "key", "name", "role" }]`. The
+role decides what a key may do:
+
+- `viewer`: read only (`GET`), except `GET /audit`.
+- `cook`: as viewer, plus `POST /recipes/:id/cook`, `POST /batches/:id/waste`,
+  `POST /temperatures` and `POST /stocktakes/:id/counts`.
+- `manager`: everything, including `GET /audit`.
+
+A request without a key or with an unknown key answers 401 `unauthorized`;
+a known key without permission answers 403 `forbidden`. The keys in
+`data/seed.json` (`dev-viewer-key`, `dev-cook-key`, `dev-manager-key`) are
+for development only.
+
+## Audit
+
+Every non-`GET` request made with a known key (whatever its status) writes an
+audit entry `{ id, at, keyName, method, path, status }`. `GET /audit` lists
+them newest first (managers only).
+
